 35CL c  2006Me08: Muons were generated from the decay of 90-MeV/c |p{+-} beam  
 35CL2c  in a 6-m, 1.2-T superconducting solenoid and were selected by a bending
 35CL3c  magnet at the M9B beamline at TRIUMF. The target was 15-g natural      
 35CL4c  calcium. |g rays and x rays were detected using a 186-cm{+3} HPGe      
 35CL5c  detector. Charged particles caused by electrons from muon decay were   
 35CL6c  tagged by a plastic scintillator in front of the HPGe detector.        
 35CL7c  Measured E|g, I|g, E(x ray), I(x ray). Deduced levels, muon capture    
 35CL8c  yields.                                                                
